course: dictionary
lesson: 14944
title: Reinforced: made stronger
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Reinforced means made stronger. You can make something stronger by adding more material or support, like steel bars inside concrete.
explain: «The bridge was reinforced with steel bars.» The steel makes the bridge stronger, so reinforced means made stronger with extra material.
explain: Reinforced can also mean made stronger or surer. «Practice reinforced what we learned in class.» Practice made the learning stick, so we understood it better.
explain: Reinforced can mean given more people or supplies. «The army was reinforced when more soldiers arrived.» When you check a meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Reinforce means to make something stronger.
fact: «Reinforced» is the past tense of reinforce, and it can also be an adjective, as in «reinforced concrete».
fact: Reinforced concrete has steel bars inside it, which help it carry heavy loads.
fact: In learning, «reinforced» means made surer or stronger by practice.
fact: In stories, an army is reinforced when more troops arrive.
exercise: «The shed door was reinforced with metal strips.» What does reinforced mean here? | Made smaller | Painted bright red | *Made stronger | Taken off its hinges
exercise: «Our teacher reinforced the times tables with a quick quiz.» What does reinforced mean? | Did it very slowly | Turned it into a game with no rules | *Made the learning surer and stronger | Forgot all about it
exercise: Which word is the past tense of reinforce? | reinforce | reinforcing | *reinforced | reinforces
test: «The castle walls were reinforced with stone.» What does reinforced mean? | *Made stronger | Painted | Made weaker | Knocked down
test: «The army was reinforced when two hundred more soldiers arrived.» What does reinforced mean here? | Sent home | Made quieter | Made into a game | *Given more soldiers
exam: «Reinforced concrete has steel bars inside it, so it can hold up a heavy bridge.» Why is the concrete strong? | Because it is small | Because it is painted | *Because steel bars make it stronger | Because it is wet
